# Test queries (RTL)

Follow [test/README.md#query-priority](../../test/README.md#query-priority). Tests must resemble how users interact with the UI.

## Query order

1. `screen.getByRole` with `name` — default for almost everything
2. `getByLabelText` — forms
3. `getByText` — static copy
4. `getByTestId` — only when role/label/text cannot work

Use `within(container)` to scope queries inside a section, dialog, or list.

## Do not assert

- `toHaveClass()` or `className` — use `toBeVisible()` / `not.toBeVisible()`, ARIA attributes, or user-visible text
- `querySelector()` — use roles and accessible names
- CSS class names as selectors (`.animate-pulse`, `.text-primary`)

## Prefer user-visible state

| Instead of | Use |
|------------|-----|
| `toHaveClass('sr-only')` | `not.toBeVisible()` (label still in a11y tree) |
| `toHaveClass('text-primary')` | sorted label, `aria-current`, `aria-expanded`, selected tab/radio |
| `querySelector('.animate-pulse')` | absence of loaded content + presence of heading/status |
| Decorative icon in DOM | accessible name on the control (e.g. sr-only “Trending topic”) |

ESLint rules: `test-conventions/no-implementation-assertions`, `eslint-plugin-testing-library`.
